# Credentials for scripts/release_web.sh — copy to `.env.release` (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# ⭐ Only needed for ONE thing: the help page's video list. `site/help.js` reads the `maddie_videos`
# table at page load, so you add, replace, reorder or unpublish a clip in the Supabase dashboard and it
# lands on the next visit — no deploy (ADR-319). Without these the page still renders in full and the
# video section says it is not configured.
#
# ⚠️ Use the **anon / publishable** key — the same one the Streamlit app and the mobile binary already
# carry. NEVER the `service_role` key: it bypasses RLS, and unlike Streamlit this one is served to
# browsers. `maddie_videos` is `SELECT`-only for `anon`, which is the whole reason publishing it is safe
# (ADR-216, docs/SUPABASE_RLS.md).

# ── The easy way: the names you already have ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⭐⭐ **Paste these two verbatim** from Streamlit Cloud (Manage app → Settings → Secrets) or from
# wherever you keep them. They are the same project and the same key this repo has always used, so
# there is nothing to edit and nothing to get wrong — the script strips the table name off the URL
# itself (`…/rest/v1/squads` → `…/rest/v1`).
#
FPL_STORE_URL=https://your-ref.supabase.co/rest/v1/squads
FPL_STORE_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key

# ── The override, if you ever need a different project for the videos ─────────────────────────────
#
# These win over the pair above. ⚠️ **Unlike `FPL_STORE_URL`, this one is taken exactly as given** —
# so it must be the PostgREST base with no table on the end. Leave the table on and the hub breaks
# *silently*: the page asks for `…/rest/v1/squads/maddie_videos` and just says it could not load the
# videos. The script now refuses a URL that does not end in `/rest/v1` and tells you so, but ⭐ *the
# safest option is still the one above, which cannot be spelled wrong.*
#
# MADBOOTS_STORE_URL=https://your-ref.supabase.co/rest/v1
# MADBOOTS_STORE_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key
